    "summary": "High‑energy second set with monster The Other One and crisp Keith piano",
    "blurb": "The Oct 22 1971 Auditorium Theatre show delivers a tight, high‑octane second set highlighted by an expansive The Other One suite, vibrant Cumberland Blues and an upfront Keith Godchaux. First‑set gems include Me & Bobby McGee and Black Peter, while the band’s overall playing is inspired and well‑rehearsed. Excellent soundboard sources make this a must‑listen for 1971 fans.",
    "review": "October 22, 1971 at Chicago’s Auditorium Theatre captures the Dead in a rare moment of focused brilliance. After an uneven first set that still offers strong performances of Me & Bobby McGee and Black Peter, the band launches into a second set that feels both meticulously rehearsed and wildly improvisational. The Other One suite roars with Jerry’s soaring leads and Phil’s “bomb‑like” bass, while Keith Godchaux’s early piano work sits front‑and‑center, adding tasty texture to every transition. Highlights such as Cumberland Blues, Deal and a bright Sugar Magnolia keep the momentum rolling, and the rhythm section drives each jam with tight, propulsive energy. Both available soundboard recordings are crystal clear, but the Miller SBD of Set 2 (gd1971-10-22.set2.sbd.miller.86728.sbeok.flac16) best captures the nuance and power of this performance.",
